            <ArticleTitle>Synergistic silver/scandium catalysis for divergent synthesis of skeletally diverse chromene derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10692-10695</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc05563c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The combination of AgTFA and Sc(OTf)3 enables the bimetallic synergistic catalysis of β-alkynyl ketones and o-hydroxybenzyl alcohols, allowing divergent synthesis of three classes of skeletally diverse chromene derivatives with generally good yields and high diastereoselectivity through dehydroxylated bi- and tri-cyclization cascades. The selectivity of these cycloadditions was controlled by adjusting the catalyst loading and reaction temperatures. The mechanisms for forming these compounds were proposed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
